# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 9 (a host gives its child's result beside the element tree; a forwarding host hands the place the World's answers in their own tick) and Type System ch. 2, "Bundles": `$n` is the child's hold, read in the tick of the click, and each firing of `!inc` reaches `$seen`, a hold, in that same tick; the child's button is forwarded at `0/[0]/0`, as in ts-ch04-whole-hosted-result.
test both_parts_read

tick 0
  added:
    0/[0]/0: Ui.Button(label="inc")
    1: Ui.Label(text="0 counted, 0 seen")

tick 1
  in:
    0/[0]/0: click
  changed:
    1: Ui.Label(text="1 counted, 1 seen")

tick 2
  in:
    0/[0]/0: click
  changed:
    1: Ui.Label(text="2 counted, 2 seen")
